\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 A facility as large and as deep as Ruined Castle still depended on the surface for survival. It needs to exploit  existing caverns and relative stone density. It needed to breathe, ingest energy and eliminate waste. It needed to shed heat. It needed internal transport vehicles to carry supplies and resources, as well as the the staff who were the lifeblood for its purpose.\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 If the facility was to be kept secure, its surface tells needed to be close to undetectable, its countermeasures as good as Eloise\'92s reputation: vents shaped like tree ferns, decoy exhaust shafts, distributed air outlets, acoustic baffling, vibration isolation, electromagnetic shielding, a delta of disguised drainage outlets, artificially maintained vegetation, false rockfalls and scree slopes, concealed portals, landscaping engineered to disguise the scars of excavation and settlement\'97and a waste discharge system that, mythologically, sent it all \'93straight to Bondi\'94.\
Even so, Fridge Force had access to enough data\'97through thermal imaging, multispectral cameras
\f2\fs24 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 , 
\f1\fs22 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 gas sensors, LiDAR, synthetic aperture radar, ground-penetrating radar, acoustic microphones, seismic sensors, water-quality analysis, electromagnetic sensors\'97enough data to plot the shape and metabolism of the thing that lay like a giant goanna under blankets of rock and wild bushland, without learning much about the function or arrangement of its individual organs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 In the sky above Sublime Point, the battle between two software systems continued. The Fridge Force swarm, though depleted, continued to adapt to Eloise Shakti\'92s laser defences. The drones kept falling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Eventually a pentad of drones made it past the lasers and immediately dropped to the tree line, almost skimming gum leaves as it made for a near-invisible air-conditioning shaft in the bushland west of the hover pad. The head of the shaft was protected by a grate, a pest-control system and a cleaning mechanism that removed dead leaves and other detritus. The shaft was impassable short of blowing it up.\
The drones arranged themselves directly over the shaft site and began to circle around it\'97although 
\f3\i circling
\f1\i0  would not be a completely accurate description. Rather, they followed an elliptical locus and gradually increased to their maximum speed. Once stabilised, the drones kept making fine adjustments to their elevation and spacing between their neighbours, as if they were all following a conductor on the ground.\
If Sarah had seen them in motion, she would have noticed the parallels with the movements of the monkeys on the Washing Machine rail, and wondered if the drones carried Gyges discs.
